# Everything hardware-facing is inherited from reven:base. Only the
# colorburst delta lives here.

# The OOBE automation API and the open DevTools port (chrome_dev.conf gets
# --enable-oobe-test-api and --remote-debugging-port=9229 from the BSP).
# They exist purely so the host tooling can drive OOBE while developing.
# RELEASE BUILDS MUST SET -colorburst_devtools.
USE="${USE} colorburst_devtools"

# reven's public overlay only lists amd_ucode; ChromeOS Flex gets its real
# firmware set from Google's private BSP, which we do not have. Without this
# the image ships with no Intel Wi-Fi or Bluetooth firmware at all (found the
# hard way: the first colorburst image had a single iwlwifi file).
LINUX_FIRMWARE="${LINUX_FIRMWARE} iwlwifi-all ibt_9260 ibt_9462 ibt_9560 ibt_ax200 ibt_ax201 ibt_ax203 ibt_ax210 ibt_ax211"

# Intel GPU firmware (GuC/DMC/HuC): the 6.12 i915 driver on Tiger Lake and
# newer is much more firmware-dependent than 5.15 was. Same private-BSP hole
# as the wireless firmware above.
LINUX_FIRMWARE="${LINUX_FIRMWARE} i915_skl i915_glk i915_cnl i915_tgl i915_adl i915_mtl"

# Visible kernel console for hardware bring-up: a stock ChromeOS kernel has
# no VT, so a laptop with no serial port boots blind and every failure looks
# like "hangs at the bootloader". These fragments give kernel messages on the
# EFI framebuffer from the first moments of boot.
# RELEASE BUILDS SHOULD DROP THESE (frecon owns the screen in production).
USE="${USE} vtconsole fbconsole efi_earlycon"

# chromeos-config identity database. Without has_chromeos_config_bsp no
# chromeos-config-bsp is installed, /usr/share/chromeos-config/configfs.img
# never gets built, cros_config_setup fails at boot, the cros_configfs job
# never reaches "started", boot-splash never runs, and boot-services waits
# forever on "stopped boot-splash": the whole boot deadlocks silently after
# chromeos_startup, on real hardware and in VMs alike. reven gets its config
# from Google's private overlay; we ship the generic one like amd64-generic.
USE="${USE} unibuild has_chromeos_config_bsp"

# Do NOT apply Chromium's checked-in field trial testing config
# (testing/variations/fieldtrial_testing_config.json). That file is Chromium's
# CI matrix, not a shipping configuration, and an UNBRANDED build applies it by
# default: ShouldUseFieldTrialTestingConfig() only opts out for
# GOOGLE_CHROME_BRANDING, or when a --variations-server-url is set. We are
# neither branded nor talking to a variations server, so we got it in full --
# 784 studies matching the chromeos platform, forcing 1068 features on and 101
# off, none of them ours. Among them ExternalHDR10, which marked any
# BT.2020+PQ external monitor as HDR10 while the connector was driven in SDR
# with no HDR metadata: every such display came out washed out.
EXTRA_GN_ARGS="disable_fieldtrial_testing_config=true"
